WEBVTT

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.784
than it looks to the naked eye.

00:02:01.826 --> 00:02:02.827
(Cheers)

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:03.870
(Laughter)

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:05.037
That's right.

00:02:05.079 --> 00:02:06.956
(Laughter and applause)

00:02:06.998 --> 00:02:08.916
So how did the universe get this way,

00:02:08.958 --> 00:02:11.085
and what exactly is inside?

00:02:11.544 --> 00:02:13.087
So I'm a theoretical physicist

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:15.590
with expertise in particle cosmology.

00:02:16.591 --> 00:02:18.551
And it's my job to use math

00:02:18.551 --> 00:02:21.929
to study the origin
and evolution of space-time

00:02:21.971 --> 00:02:24.223
and every single thing
that's inside of it.

00:02:25.349 --> 00:02:29.103
I connect the very small --
elementary particles --

00:02:29.145 --> 00:02:33.274
with the extremely large --
galaxies and galaxy clusters,